---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Citation from '@components/Citation.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About">
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-thmblue mb-6">About</h1>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-thmblue mt-8 mb-3 font-sans">Author</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-800 leading-relaxed mb-3">
      <strong>Yan Senez</strong>, born in 1979, is an artist, independent
      researcher, image technician, polymath, tinkerer, weekend coder, and
      stubbornly curious mind. Trained in physical sciences, he works outside
      academic affiliation, at the border between visual experimentation,
      computation, technical improvisation, and theoretical exploration.
    </p>
    <p class="text-stone-800 leading-relaxed mb-3">
      As a teenager reading Mark A. Ludwig and thinking about the emergence
      of complex structures from simple rules, he became fascinated by the
      Ulam spiral: the image in which prime numbers reveal an unexpected
      geometric structure. PT grew from that intuition: prime numbers may be
      the simplest, and most demanding, system for testing whether an elementary
      constraint can produce persistent organization.
    </p>
    <p class="text-stone-800 leading-relaxed mb-3">
      In 2025, that older thread met an analysis of noise and information
      alteration in an image, then grew into an 883-page English monograph
      and a 913-page French monograph. Details of the genesis are in the
      <a href="/en/monograph" class="underline text-thmblue">preface</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-thmblue mt-8 mb-3 font-sans">Contact</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-800 leading-relaxed">
      Email: <a href="mailto:yan.senez@protonmail.com" class="underline text-thmblue">yan.senez@protonmail.com</a><br />
      GitHub: <a href="https://github.com/Igrekess" class="underline text-thmblue">github.com/Igrekess</a><br />
      Dedicated page: <a href="/en/contact" class="underline text-thmblue">form and other channels</a>
    </p>

    <Citation lang="en" />

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-thmblue mt-8 mb-3 font-sans">Editorial status</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-800 leading-relaxed mb-3">
      Preprint. <strong>Not peer-reviewed.</strong> The author welcomes critical
      scrutiny and independent verification. The 59 computational verification
      scripts are public and reproducible.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-thmblue mt-8 mb-3 font-sans">Licences</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Item</th><th>Licence</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Site code (Astro, JS, configs)</td><td>MIT</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Site editorial content</td><td>CC BY 4.0</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Monograph (PDF EN + FR)</td><td>CC BY 4.0</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Thematic article PDFs</td><td>CC BY 4.0</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Python verification scripts</td><td>MIT</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-thmblue mt-8 mb-3 font-sans">Credits</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-800 leading-relaxed text-sm">
      Built with <a href="https://astro.build" class="underline">Astro</a>,
      <a href="https://tailwindcss.com" class="underline">Tailwind CSS</a>,
      <a href="https://katex.org" class="underline">KaTeX</a>.
      Hosting: GitHub Pages. Domain: <code>www.persistencetheory.org</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
